    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.animate\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nWith vim.opt.scrolloff = 9999 and some remapping like 'k' to 'kzz' cursor stays in the middle of the screen even if there is no text below it. However, with mini.animate scroll enabled cursor is bound to bottom of the screen if there is no teхt below it.\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to have an option for mini.animate to allow the cursor to stay centered?",
    "closed_at": "2024-08-06T07:36:52Z",
