    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nScrolling animation (and resize, for that matter) are suboptimal because they are done with side-effects. See [this section](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/af673d8523c5c2c5ff0a53b1e42a296ca358dcc7/doc/mini-animate.txt#L279-L295), which also has a note about special overrides of `nnoremap n nzvzz` and why they don't really work.\r\n\r\nHaving special option for cursor always being centered seems both too specific and not trivial to implement. At the same time, the current implementation is as best as I can do to support non-default 'scrolloff' value.\r\n\r\nClosing as \"not planned because it is already as best as it can be under current design\".",
            "created_at": "2024-08-06T07:36:52Z",
